# ── .git moved out of iCloud sync scope (2026-09-20) ────────────────────────
# `~/Documents` is inside macOS Desktop & Documents sync. iCloud makes a
# "conflict copy" named `<file> 2` when it cannot reconcile two versions of a
# file, and git's write pattern provokes exactly that: `.git/index` is rewritten
# in place constantly, and refs are written then renamed atomically. In
# portfolio_tracker a copy of `refs/remotes/origin/main` appeared as `main 2`
# and broke `git push` outright ("fatal: bad object"). Files whose NAME ends in
# `.nosync` are skipped by iCloud, so the real git directory is `.git.nosync`
# and `.git` is a symlink to it. Git follows the symlink and behaves normally.
#
# This line is load-bearing: without it git sees `.git.nosync/` as untracked
# working-tree content and `git add -A` would try to commit the whole object
# database into itself.
.git.nosync/
